{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-01T10:09:22.335Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-01T10:09:22.335Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-01T10:09:22.335Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Public API audit: node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/lock/lock.d.ts:109,118 expose acquireLock(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...) and acquireLockLease(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...), with no directory handle or filesystem capability parameter. sdk/workspace-transaction.d.ts:43-63 likewise accepts a string pmRoot and no filesystem provider. Native stale cleanup opens its owner path after awaited pathname operations. The latest inspected public SDK has the same limitation. Upstream issue search for symlink lock returned no matching open issue; no issue was filed. pm-cli#1620 concerns ordinary writers and is not evidence of path confinement. This dependency remains an unresolved blocking P1, not an approved scope deferral."}]}],"before_hash":"6e481ba406d06cb5a09c00a2ab66dcd618ccfbd90b87d5582280a4eb50efe504","after_hash":"d3c3d6187b1eefdef960f10bedff880d93edc23a88c93400dd43e8e499e57d98","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c4998001120429cda23d59ccf68f2cbf0d92832337b65a76dc8bc6f4d8c55fc0"}
