{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T05:42:26.971Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"76ccb4e1548ff983ee831367","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-02T05:42:26.971Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Started from pulled head 4d98fdb and read PR 107 plus cubic thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3. Registry reports SDK 2026.11.2 published 2026-11-02T05:26:13.578Z; its Security changelog names GH-1647. Plan: refresh dev/peer/manifest pins and both lockfiles, map lock_path_unsafe to the package boundary refusal, add native acquisition and command regressions with an old-SDK negative control, restore evidence-backed documentation, and run focused coverage plus requested gates. Published lock-confinement declarations say a lock created during a late directory replacement is deliberately retained outside the tracker; that differs from the supplied removal precondition and must be reproduced before claiming the broader original acceptance criteria."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T05:42:26.971Z"}],"before_hash":"75a2c08d153d3dfb35e5396c5f85dc3028c7117ac6fcf00b8554043c09746c7e","after_hash":"62d868d55b160365d9624a254c2d3fc2b7440c5fb5c77fe748a518fb8bbfdca3","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"374eed551960b683b99e6c5c82df4b445b4ceac324d2de8fabf79ebcc40a1deb"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T05:47:57.606Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"76ccb4e1548ff983ee831367","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-02T05:47:57.602Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Published-SDK behavior is now reproduced in test/sdk-lock-confinement.test.ts: raw acquireLock/acquireLockLease refuse static locks symlinks with lock_path_unsafe/4; all three package acquisition paths refuse the original mkdir substitution with rl_state_path_invalid/2 and leave no outside lock. A second real fs/promises interleaving replaces locks immediately at open(wx): SDK 2026.11.2 refuses with lock_path_unsafe/4 but leaves confined.lock outside, zero bytes. Its own lock-confinement declarations explicitly retain that file because pathname unlink could remove an unrelated replacement. Therefore the supplied stray-removal precondition is false and the original broader no-follow/no-outside-write acceptance cannot honestly be completed. Keeping that criterion open while finishing the bounded adoption and verification."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T05:47:57.606Z"}],"before_hash":"62d868d55b160365d9624a254c2d3fc2b7440c5fb5c77fe748a518fb8bbfdca3","after_hash":"f703ecd2a73c71ad57987dbf2df0af8b96b3f9a80171d71a13559f054cb60bf7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"recor